  "title": "More vowels",
  "teTitle": "అచ్చులు 2",
  "cefr": "A0",
  "register": "standard",
  "description": "Finish the vowels: ఎ ఏ ఐ ఒ ఓ ఔ, plus the hum అం and the puff అః.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "u82-i01",
      "te": "ఎ",
      "audioTe": "ఎ. ఎద్దు.",
      "gloss": "e — as in 'eddu' (bull)",
      "words": [{ "te": "ఎ", "gloss": "short 'e', like the e in 'end'" }],
      "tags": ["vowel"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u82-i02"],
      "note": "ఎ and ఏ are twins — ఏ grows an extra check-mark on top. Spot that mark before you read."
    },
    {
      "id": "u82-i02",
      "te": "ఏ",
      "audioTe": "ఏ. ఏనుగు.",
      "gloss": "ee — as in 'eenugu' (elephant)",
      "words": [{ "te": "ఏ", "gloss": "long 'ee', like the a in 'gate' held longer" }],
      "tags": ["vowel"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u82-i01"],
      "note": "You already ask ఏ ఊరు? (which town?) and ఏంటి? (what?) — both start with this long ఏ."
    },
    {
      "id": "u82-i03",
      "te": "ఐ",
      "audioTe": "ఐ. ఐదు.",
      "gloss": "ai — as in 'aidu' (five)",
      "words": [{ "te": "ఐ", "gloss": "'ai', like the i in 'time'" }],
      "tags": ["vowel"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u82-i06", "u82-i01"],
      "note": "Careful later: ఐ also looks a lot like the consonant బ (ba). The vowel ఐ has the extra loop below."
    },
    {
      "id": "u82-i04",
      "te": "ఒ",
      "audioTe": "ఒ. ఒకటి.",
      "gloss": "o — as in 'okaTi' (one)",
      "words": [{ "te": "ఒ", "gloss": "short 'o', like the o in 'obey'" }],
      "tags": ["vowel"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u82-i05", "u82-i06"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u82-i05",
      "te": "ఓ",
      "audioTe": "ఓ. ఓడ.",
      "gloss": "oo — as in 'ooDa' (ship)",
      "words": [{ "te": "ఓ", "gloss": "long 'oo', like the o in 'go' held longer" }],
      "tags": ["vowel"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u82-i04", "u82-i06"],
      "note": "ఒ ఓ ఔ are a family: ఓ adds a top mark to ఒ, and ఔ adds a tail after it. Three lookalikes — the marks decide."
    },
    {
      "id": "u82-i06",
      "te": "ఔ",
      "audioTe": "ఔ. ఔను.",
      "gloss": "au — as in 'aunu' (yes)",
      "words": [{ "te": "ఔ", "gloss": "'au', like the ow in 'cow'" }],
      "tags": ["vowel"],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "distractors": ["u82-i05", "u82-i03"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u82-i07",
      "te": "అం",
      "audioTe": "అం. అందం.",
      "gloss": "am — అ with the round sunna (dot)",
      "words": [{ "te": "అం", "gloss": "am — the circle ం adds a nasal hum" }],
      "tags": ["sign"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "distractors": ["u81-i01", "u82-i08"],
      "note": "That little circle ం is the సున్న (sunna). It hums like m or n: అందం (beauty), అన్నం (rice). You will see it everywhere."
    },
    {
      "id": "u82-i08",
      "te": "అః",
      "audioTe": "అః. దుఃఖం.",
      "gloss": "aha — అ with the two-dot visarga",
      "words": [{ "te": "అః", "gloss": "aha — the two dots ః add a breathy 'h' puff" }],
      "tags": ["sign"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "distractors": ["u82-i07", "u81-i01"],
      "note": "ః (visarga) is rare — mostly in Sanskrit loans like దుఃఖం (sorrow). Recognize it; you'll seldom write it."
    },
    {
